# ==============================================================================
# AgentPulse Mosquitto ACL Sample Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# This configuration demonstrates least-privilege Access Control Lists (ACLs)
# for securing MQTT communication in AgentPulse v1 / release-0.4.0+.
#
# References:
#   - docs/mqtt-protocol.md §6.2 (Security Hardening: TLS & ACL)
#   - Mosquitto ACL format documentation: https://mosquitto.org/man/mosquitto-conf-5.html
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   1. Replace placeholder user accounts (operator-alice, node-mac-studio) with
#      your actual deployment usernames or client certificate Common Names.
#   2. Never commit real credentials, passwords, or production network addresses
#      to source control.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Operator & Monitor Clients (`agentpulse watch`, `agentpulse list`, `dispatch`)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identity: operator-{user} (e.g. operator-alice, operator-bob)
#
# Permissions:
#   - Read all machine heartbeats and online statuses:
#   - Read all job lifecycle state transitions:
#   - Read task execution console log streams:
#   - Write dispatch instructions to worker machines:
#   - Read/write system notifications and alerts:

user operator-alice
topic read agentpulse/v1/machines/+/status
topic read agentpulse/v1/machines/+/jobs/+/status
topic read agentpulse/v1/machines/+/jobs/+/logs
topic read agentpulse/v1/+/announce
topic write agentpulse/v1/machines/+/commands/dispatch
topic readwrite agentpulse/v1/notifications/alerts

user operator-bob
topic read agentpulse/v1/machines/+/status
topic read agentpulse/v1/machines/+/jobs/+/status
topic read agentpulse/v1/machines/+/jobs/+/logs
topic read agentpulse/v1/+/announce
topic write agentpulse/v1/machines/+/commands/dispatch
topic readwrite agentpulse/v1/notifications/alerts

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Worker Nodes (Thin Wrapper & Listener Daemons)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identity: node-{machine_id} (e.g. node-mac-studio, node-linux-gpu)
#
# Permissions:
#   - Read and write ONLY within their own machine topic sub-tree.
#   - Workers cannot spoof heartbeats or status updates of other nodes.
#   - Workers cannot eavesdrop on other machines' dispatch commands or log streams.
#   - Optional write permission to system notifications for urgent alerts.

# Worker Node 1: mac-studio
user node-mac-studio
topic readwrite agentpulse/v1/machines/mac-studio/#
topic readwrite agentpulse/v1/mac-studio/announce
topic write agentpulse/v1/notifications/alerts

# Worker Node 2: linux-gpu
user node-linux-gpu
topic readwrite agentpulse/v1/machines/linux-gpu/#
topic readwrite agentpulse/v1/linux-gpu/announce
topic write agentpulse/v1/notifications/alerts

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Dynamic Pattern Matching Alternative (Mosquitto 1.5+)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When worker nodes authenticate using usernames matching their machine ID,
# or when using mTLS client certificates where the Common Name matches %u,
# the pattern directive enables automatic per-machine isolation without manually
# enumerating every node identity:
#
# pattern readwrite agentpulse/v1/machines/%u/#
# pattern readwrite agentpulse/v1/%u/announce
# pattern write agentpulse/v1/notifications/alerts
